        "original_id": "a3c1cae9-52e3-5edd-979b-6ca5da82124e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Philip Quast, Colm Wilkinson, Michael Ball, Lea Salonga, Judy Kuhn, Ruthie Henshall, Michael Maguire, Alun Armstrong, Jenny Galloway, Adam Searles, Hannah Chick, John Caird, David Charles Abell\n- Productions: Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert, London production, Broadway production, Australian production\n- Organizations: Royal Philharmonic Orchestra\n- Roles: Jean Valjean, Inspector Javert, Marius Pontmercy, Éponine, Cosette, Fantine, Enjolras, Thénardier, Madame Thénardier, Gavroche, Young Cosette\n- Awards: Laurence Olivier Award for Best Actor in a Musical\n\nFacts:\n- Philip Mark Quast was born on 30 July 1957 and is an Australian actor and singer.\n- The 10th Anniversary cast of Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert starred Colm Wilkinson as Jean Valjean, Philip Quast as Inspector Javert, Michael Ball as Marius Pontmercy, Lea Salonga as Éponine, Judy Kuhn as Cosette, Ruthie Henshall as Fantine, Michael Maguire as Enjolras, Alun Armstrong as Thénardier, Jenny Galloway as Madame Thénardier, Adam Searles as Gavroche, and Hannah Chick as Young Cosette.\n- Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert was directed by John Caird.\n- The performers in Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert were chosen from the London, Broadway, and Australian productions of the show.\n- The Royal Philharmonic Orchestra in Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert was conducted by David Charles Abell.\n- Philip Quast has won the Laurence Olivier Award for Best Actor in a Musical three times, which is the most of any actor to date.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
